WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.260
A candidate title, an introduction route, and a signed license are three different states.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:11.410
VERION should describe a right as secured only after the agreement is signed and effective.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.172
All counts and negotiation claims require documentary evidence during due diligence.

00:00:16.272 --> 00:00:20.980
An IP license must define content, functions, territory, language, and duration.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:25.729
Quiz, card, advertising, exhibition, AI, and secondary-trading rights are not interchangeable.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:30.050
Anything outside the signed scope remains unavailable until separately approved.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:36.151
VERION plans to prioritize titles by fan interest, licensing feasibility, cost, and product fit.

00:00:36.181 --> 00:00:40.181
A famous title is not automatically the best first agreement.

00:00:40.211 --> 00:00:45.651
The priority model is an internal decision tool, not evidence that any rights holder will agree.

00:00:45.751 --> 00:00:50.050
The agreement must define approvals, reporting, takedown, and end-of-term handling.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.222
Minimum guarantees and advances should match the licensed scope and validated demand.

00:00:55.252 --> 00:01:01.256
Long duration or exclusivity is valuable only when the obligations remain affordable and executable.

00:01:01.356 --> 00:01:07.354
Before signing, VERION must verify the rights chain, authority, existing conflicts, and usable materials.

00:01:07.384 --> 00:01:11.784
Ownership of a physical item does not grant copyright or digital-use rights.

00:01:11.814 --> 00:01:17.334
No title or asset should appear as official before the rights ledger and approval record are complete.

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:23.034
The current equity seed plan allocates one hundred fifty million yen to IP licensing.

00:01:23.064 --> 00:01:26.824
That is a planning ceiling, not a commitment to spend the full amount.

00:01:26.854 --> 00:01:32.854
Capital should be released in stages only when scope, cost, timing, and approvals are acceptable.

00:01:32.954 --> 00:01:38.105
A portfolio requires title-level records of rights, obligations, cost, and operating results.

00:01:38.135 --> 00:01:43.686
The company should monitor concentration by rights holder, title, region, and revenue source.

00:01:43.716 --> 00:01:48.423
Renewal, expansion, reduction, or exit should follow evidence for each agreement.

00:01:48.523 --> 00:01:54.584
The objective is not the largest title count, but usable rights under executable terms.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:58.934
VERION must prove compliance and operating value title by title.

00:01:58.964 --> 00:02:04.113
License acquisition, renewal, exclusivity, transfer value, and future revenue are not guaranteed.
